@startuml
title The same workflow as a v2 statechart and as its lossy SCXML projection
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Workflow v2 semantics" as V2 #E9F5EA {
  state "Classify" as V2Classify #DCEEFF
  [*] --> V2Classify
  state "Summarize" as V2Sum #DCEEFF
  state "Escalate" as V2Esc #DCEEFF
  V2Classify --> V2Sum : completed [priority 0]\nurgency low (first match)
  V2Classify --> V2Esc : completed [priority 1]\nurgency high
  state "Draft" as V2Draft #DCEEFF
  V2Sum --> V2Draft : completed
  V2Esc --> V2Draft : completed
  V2Draft --> V2Draft : needsWork [<latex>\kappa < 3</latex>] / <latex>\kappa{+}{+}</latex>
  state "QuorumJoin\n(2 of 3 reviewers)" as V2Join #FFE0C8
  V2Draft --> V2Join : completed (all-match fan-out\nto three reviewers, then quorum)
  state "Publish" as V2Pub #D9EFDF
  V2Join --> V2Pub : completed [<latex>|\mathrm{dom}\, j| \ge 2</latex>]
  V2Pub --> [*]
}

state "SCXML projection (lossy)" as SC #DCEEFF {
  state "Classify " as SCClassify #DCEEFF
  [*] --> SCClassify
  state "Summarize " as SCSum #DCEEFF
  state "Escalate " as SCEsc #DCEEFF
  SCClassify --> SCSum : disposition.completed.classify\n[cond: urgency low] (document order)
  SCClassify --> SCEsc : disposition.completed.classify\n(later in document order)
  state "Draft " as SCDraft #F8DADA
  SCSum --> SCDraft : disposition.completed.summarize
  SCEsc --> SCDraft : disposition.completed.escalate
  SCDraft --> SCDraft : disposition.needsWork.draft\n(datamodel counter: GLOBAL, not token-local)
  state "Reviewers " as SCJoin #F8DADA
  SCDraft --> SCJoin : disposition.completed.draft\n(single configuration: no simultaneous\nthree-reviewer fan-out)
  state "Publish " as SCPub #D9EFDF
  SCJoin --> SCPub : done.state.reviewers\n(all regions final; NO 2-of-3 quorum)
  SCPub --> [*]
}

note bottom of SC #FDECEA
Red-bordered states mark projection loss:
the token-local bound <latex>\kappa</latex> becomes a global datamodel
counter, all-match fan-out inside one region is not
representable in a single configuration, and quorum,
race, reduce joins, noMatch policies, and durable
yields have no SCXML counterpart.
end note
note bottom of V2 #EAF7EE
Explicit unique priorities replace SCXML document
order; dispositions are token-local triggers, not
queued events. The construct-by-construct mapping
is the SCXML correspondence design document.
end note
@enduml
